{"lines": ["On the fourth of October, 1967, at about eleven twenty at night, something was reported crashing into the water off Shag Harbour, a small fishing village on Nova Scotia's Atlantic coast.", "At least eleven people saw a low, lit object head toward the harbour. Several heard a whistling sound, then a whoosh, then a loud bang.", "The first call came from a local resident, Laurie Wickens, and four friends driving on Highway 3. They watched the object settle on the water, two hundred fifty to three hundred metres offshore.", "Wickens phoned the RCMP and reported that a large aircraft had crashed. Within about fifteen minutes, two officers arrived, expecting survivors.", "They asked the Rescue Coordination Centre in Halifax whether any aircraft was missing. Canadian civilian and military agencies took part, and so did the American Condon Committee.", "The object was never officially identified. Canadian government documents simply call it an unidentified flying object.", "That night was not the first strange sight. Earlier, Air Canada Flight 305 had reported a lit rectangular object keeping pace beside the plane, with a string of smaller lights behind it.", "Near Halifax, a fishing captain, Leo Mersey, watched four stationary blips on his radar. Then he looked up and saw four bright objects in the sky.", "A single witness gives you a story. Many witnesses give you a case."], "words": [["On", 0.0, 0.12], ["the", 0.12, 0.22], ["fourth", 0.22, 0.7], ["of", 0.7, 0.75], ["October,", 0.75, 1.22], ["1967,", 1.22, 1.84], ["at", 3.12, 3.24], ["about", 3.24, 3.48], ["eleven", 3.48, 3.96], ["twenty", 3.96, 4.44], ["at", 4.44, 4.68], ["night,", 4.68, 4.92], ["something", 5.28, 5.54], ["was", 5.54, 5.78], ["reported", 5.78, 6.24], ["crashing", 6.24, 6.72], ["into", 6.72, 7.26], ["the", 7.26, 7.38], ["water", 7.38, 7.74], ["off", 7.74, 8.0], ["Shag", 8.0, 8.4], ["Harbour,", 8.4, 9.12], ["a", 9.12, 9.28], ["small", 9.28, 9.56], ["fishing", 9.56, 10.0], ["village", 10.0, 10.4